```lean
import Poincare.D13.HeatKernelBridge.PredicateSemantics

namespace Poincare.D13.HeatKernelBridge
open MeasureTheory Filter
open scoped Topology
open Poincare.D11.HeatKernelBridge
open Poincare.D12.HeatDomain
open Poincare.D7.HeatKernel
open Poincare.D10.HeatKernelEuclidean

variable {M : Type*} [TopologicalSpace M] [MeasurableSpace M]

/-- Version tag of the PDE-corrected D7 predicate. -/
def IsHeatKernelPDE.v2 : ℕ := 2

/-- **The D7 heat-kernel predicate with the heat equation repaired to the genuine PDE (v2).**
Same as `IsHeatKernel`/`IsHeatKernelV1` except that the `solves` field is
`HasDerivAt (fun s => K x y s) (S.laplacian (fun z => K z y t) x) t` — the pointwise
`∂_t K = Δ K` in the time variable, exactly the field of the D11 `HeatKernelCore` — rather than the
snapshot operator identity `S.timeDerivative (fun x => K x y t) = S.laplacian (fun x => K x y t)`
(whose exact content is characterized in `PredicateSemantics.lean`). The Dirac condition is stated
against an admissible test-function class, i.e. on the D12-corrected domain. `S.timeDerivative` is
retained by the ambient `HeatSpacetime` structure but is not used by this predicate. -/
